hadiths[98]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1429","On the authority of Anas, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The last person to enter Paradise is a man. He will walk once and stumble once, and the Fire will scorch him once. When he has passed beyond it, he will turn to it and say: 'Blessed is He Who has saved me from you. Allah has given me something He has not given to anyone among the first and the last.'Then a tree will be raised for him, and he will say: 'O my Lord! Bring me near to this tree so that I may take shelter in its shade and drink of its water.' Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'O son of Adam! Perhaps if I give you this, you will ask Me for something else?' He will say: 'No, O my Lord,' and he will promise Him that he will not ask for anything else. His Lord will excuse him because He sees that he has no patience for what he beholds. So He will bring him near to it, and he will take shelter in its shade and drink of its water.Then another tree, better than the first, will be raised for him, and he will say: 'O my Lord! Bring me near to this one so that I may drink of its water and take shelter in its shade; I shall not ask You for anything else.' He will say: 'O son of Adam! Did you not promise Me that you would not ask Me for anything else?' He will say: 'Perhaps if I bring you near to it, you will ask Me for something else?' So he will promise Him that he will not ask for anything else. His Lord will excuse him because He sees that he has no patience for what he beholds. So He will bring him near to it, and he will take shelter in its shade and drink of its water.Then a tree at the gate of Paradise, better than the first two, will be raised for him, and he will say: 'O my Lord! Bring me near to this one so that I may take shelter in its shade and drink of its water; I shall not ask You for anything else.' He will say: 'O son of Adam! Did you not promise Me that you would not ask Me for anything else?' He will say: 'Yes, O my Lord, this one I shall not ask You for anything else.' His Lord will excuse him because He sees that he has no patience for what he beholds. So He will bring him near to it. When He has brought him near to it, he will hear the voices of the people of Paradise, and he will say: 'O my Lord! Admit me into it.' He will say: 'O son of Adam! What will make you stop asking from Me? Would it please you if I gave you the world and the like of it with it?' He will say: 'O my Lord! Are You mocking me when You are the Lord of the Worlds?'Ibn Mas'ud laughed and said: 'Will you not ask me why I am laughing?' They said: 'Why are you laughing?' He said: 'Thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) laugh.' They said: 'Why are you laughing, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'At the laughter of the Lord of the Worlds when He said: ""Are You mocking me when You are the Lord of the Worlds?"" He will say: ""I am not mocking you, but I am Able to do whatever I will.""' — And in a narration: 'Capable.'"""
"1430","On the authority of Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ""Two men came to me, took hold of my upper arms, and brought me to a rugged mountain. They said: 'Ascend.' I said: 'I cannot manage it.' They said: 'We will make it easy for you.' So I ascended until, when I was in the middle of the mountain, I heard terrible voices. I said: 'What are these voices?' They said: 'This is the howling of the people of the Fire.' Then they proceeded with me, and behold, there were people hanging by their heels, their jaw corners torn, their jaw corners flowing with blood. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are those who break their fast before the permissible time of their fast.' Then he said: 'May the Jews and Christians fail.' Sulaymān said: 'I do not know whether Abū Umāmah heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or if it is something from his own opinion.' Then they proceeded with me, and behold, there were people with the most swollen bellies, the most foul odor, and the most repulsive appearance. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the slain of the disbelievers.' Then they proceeded with me, and behold, there were people with the most severe punishment and the most foul odor, as if their odor were that of menstrual blood. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the male and female fornicators.' Then they proceeded with me, and behold, there were women whose breasts were being bitten by snakes. I said: 'What is the matter with these?' It was said: 'These are those who withhold their milk from their children.' Then he proceeded with me, and behold, there were boys playing between two rivers. I said: 'Who are these?' They said: 'These are the offspring of the believers.' Then they elevated me to a high place, and behold, there were three men drinking from a vessel they had. I said: 'Who are these?' They said: 'These are Ja'far, Zayd, and Ibn Rawāḥah.' Then they elevated me to another high place, and behold, there were three men. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'This is Ibrāhīm, Mūsā, and 'Īsā, and they are waiting for you.'"""
"1431","[AI-translation] Aas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) came out to us with two books in his hand, and he said: Do you know what these two books are? We said: No, O Messenger of Allah, unless you inform us. He said regarding the one in his right hand: This is a book from the Lord of the Worlds, in it are the names of the people of Paradise, and the names of their fathers and their tribes, then it is concluded at the end of them, so no one is added to them and none is decreased from them ever. Then he said regarding the one in his left hand: This is a book from the Lord of the Worlds, in it are the names of the people of the Fire, and the names of their fathers and their tribes, then it is concluded at the end of them, so no one is added to them and none is decreased from them. His companions said: So what is the point of action, O Messenger of Allah, if a matter has already been concluded? He said: Be upright and draw near, for the companion of Paradise is sealed for him with the deed of the people of Paradise, even if he does any deed, and the companion of the Fire is sealed for him with the deed of the people of the Fire, even if he does any deed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) gestured with his hands and cast them, then said: Your Lord has finished with the servants, a group in Paradise and a group in the Blazing Fire."
"1432","Abdullah said: We were with the Prophet, peace be upon him, in a tent when he said: ""Would you be pleased to be one-fourth of the people of Paradise?"" We said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Would you be pleased to be one-third of the people of Paradise?"" We said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Would you be pleased to be half of the people of Paradise?"" We said: ""Yes."" He said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise, and that is because Paradise will not be entered except by a Muslim soul, and you are not among the people of polytheism except like a white hair on the skin of a black bull, or like a black hair on the skin of a red bull."""
"1433","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to me: Do you know the first group to enter Paradise from my Ummah? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The Emigrants will come on the Day of Resurrection to the gate of Paradise and will seek to enter, so the keepers will say to them: Have you been called to account? They will say: Called to account for what? For our swords were on our shoulders in the path of Allah until we died upon that. He said: So it will be opened for them, and they will stay in it for forty years before the people enter it."
"1434","[AI-translation] From Abu Bakrah, that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: When a man points a weapon at his brother, they are both on the brink of Hell, so if he kills him, they both fall into it together."
"1435","On the authority of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the believers are delivered from the Fire on the Day of Resurrection and are safe, none of you will dispute with his companion concerning a right he has against him in this world more intensely than the believers will dispute with their Lord concerning their brothers who were admitted into the Fire. They will say: 'Our Lord, our brothers used to pray with us, fast with us, and perform Hajj with us, yet You admitted them into the Fire?' He will say: 'Go and bring out those whom you recognize.' So they will come to them and recognize them by their faces, for the Fire will not consume their faces. Among them will be those whom the Fire has seized up to halfway up their shins, and among them those whom it has seized up to their ankles. They will bring them out and say: 'Our Lord, we have brought out those whom You commanded us to bring out.' Then He will say: 'Bring out those who have in their hearts the weight of a dinar of faith,' then those who have the weight of half a dinar, until He says: 'Those who have in their hearts the weight of an atom (dharrah) of faith.' Abu Sa'id said: 'Whoever does not believe this, let him read this verse: ""Indeed, Allah does not wrong [even] an atom's weight; and if there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward"" (An-Nisa: 40).' Then they will say: 'Our Lord, we have brought out those whom You commanded us to bring out, and there remains in the Fire none who has any good in him.' Then Allah will say: 'The angels have interceded, the prophets have interceded, and the believers have interceded, and there remains the Most Merciful of the merciful.' He will then take a handful from the Fire—or he said: two handfuls—of people who never did any good for Allah at all, who have been burnt until they became charcoal. They will be brought to a water called the Water of Life, and it will be poured over them, and they will sprout as the seed sprouts in the silt left by a flood. They will emerge from their bodies like pearls, with seals on their necks reading: 'The freed ones of Allah.' It will be said to them: 'Enter Paradise; whatever you wish for or see, it is yours, and with Me is even better than that.' They will say: 'Our Lord, what is better than that?' He will say: 'My pleasure upon you, so that I shall never be angry with you after this.'"""
"1436","[AI-translation] From Jabir bin Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: Do you desire anything that I may give you more? They will say: Our Lord, and what is above what You have given us? He said: So He will say: My good pleasure is greater."
"1437","[AI-translation] Irbad bin Sariyah, raised to the Prophet: When you ask Allah, ask Him for Al-Firdaus, for it is the secret of Paradise."
"1438","On the authority of Masrūq, who said: We asked ʿAbdullāh (ibn Masʿūd) about this verse. He said: ""Have we not already been asked about this?"" Then he said: ""The souls of the martyrs are in the crops of green birds, which have lanterns suspended from the Throne. They roam freely in Paradise wherever they wish, then they take refuge in those lanterns. Their Lord looked upon them and said: 'Do you desire anything?' They said: 'What could we desire, when we roam in Paradise wherever we wish?' He did this with them three times. When they realized that they would not be left without being asked, they said: 'O Lord! We wish that You return our souls to our bodies so that we may be killed in Your cause once more.' When He saw that they had no need, they were left."""
"1439","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, raised to the Prophet: The children of the Muslims are on a mountain in Paradise; Ibrahim and Sarah take care of them until they hand them over to their fathers on the Day of Resurrection."
"1440","[AI-translation] From Abu Malik who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, was asked about the children of the polytheists. He said: They are the servants of the people of Paradise."
"1441","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik that he recited this verse: He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""I was given Al-Kawthar, and it is a flowing river (thus upon the face of the earth) that was not carved out. Its two banks are domes of pearl. I struck my hand to its soil, and it was fragrant musk, and its pebbles were pearls."
"1442","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik that he recited this verse: He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""I was given Al-Kawthar, and it is a flowing river (thus upon the face of the earth) that was not carved out. Its two banks are domes of pearl. I struck my hand to its soil, and it was fragrant musk, and its pebbles were pearls."
"1443","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, marfu': ""Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? They are the weak and the oppressed. Shall I not inform you of the people of the Fire? Every harsh, obstinate person."
"1444","[AI-translation] From Suraqa ibn Malik, marfu': ""Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? The subdued, the weak. And the people of the Fire: every harsh, corpulent, arrogant person."
"1445","[AI-translation] Khudri, marfu': ""As for the people of the Fire who are its people (and in a narration: those whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, does not want to bring out), they neither die in it nor live. But there are people whom the Fire strikes due to their sins (and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, wants to bring them out), so He causes them to die a death until, when they are charcoal, permission for intercession is given. They are brought in groups, group by group, and scattered upon the rivers of Paradise. Then it is said: 'O people of Paradise! Pour upon them!' So they sprout like the sprouting of a seed that is in the flood debris."
"1446","[AI-translation] From Abu Ayyub who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I love horses; are there horses in Paradise?"" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""If you enter Paradise, you will be brought a horse of ruby with two wings; you will be mounted upon it, and it will fly with you wherever you wish."
"1447","[AI-translation] Khudri that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is a man whose face Allah turned away from the Fire towards Paradise. A tree with shade was made to appear to him, so he said: 'O my Lord, bring me forward to this tree so I may be in its shade.' Allah said: 'Perhaps if I do so, you will ask me for other than it?' He said: 'No, by Your Might!' So Allah brought him forward to it, and a tree with shade and fruit was made to appear to him. He said: 'O my Lord, bring me forward to this tree so I may be in its shade and eat from its fruit.' Allah said to him: 'Perhaps if I give you that, you will ask me for other than it?' He will say: 'No, by Your Might.' So Allah will bring him forward to it. Then another tree with shade, fruit, and water will be made to appear to him. He will say: 'O my Lord, bring me forward to this tree so I may be in its shade, eat from its fruit, and drink from its water.' He will say to him: 'Perhaps if I do so, you will ask me for other than it?' He will say: 'No, by Your Might, I will not ask you for other than it.' So Allah will bring him forward to it. Then the gate of Paradise will be presented to him, and he will say: 'O my Lord, bring me forward to the gate of Paradise so I may be beneath the portal of Paradise and look at its people.' So Allah will bring him forward to it, and he will see the people of Paradise and what is in it, and he will say: 'O my Lord, enter me into Paradise.' He said: So Allah will enter him into Paradise. He said: When he enters Paradise, he will say: 'This is for me?!' He said: Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say to him: 'Wish.' So he will wish, and Allah will remind him: 'Ask for such and such,' until his wishes are exhausted. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'It is yours and ten times its like.' He said: Then he will enter Paradise; his two wives from the houris will enter upon him and will say to him: 'Praise be to Allah who revived you for us and revived us for you.' He will say: 'No one was given the likes of what I was given.' He said: And the least of the people of the Fire in punishment will be shod with two shoes of fire, causing his brain to boil from the heat of his shoes."
"1448","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, intends mercy for a nation of His servants, He takes their prophet before them, making him a forerunner and a precursor before them. And when He intends the destruction of a nation, He punishes them while their prophet is alive, destroying it while he looks on, pleasing his eye by its destruction when they belied him and disobeyed his command."
"1449","[AI-translation] Khudri, marfu': ""Allah, Mighty and Majestic, brings a people out of the Fire after nothing remains of them in it except their faces, and Allah enters them into Paradise."
"1450","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, raising it to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), he said: ""Indeed, Allah raises the offspring of the believer to his degree, even if they fall short of him in deeds, so that his eyes may be cooled by them."" Then he recited: ""And those who believed and whose descendants followed them in faith"" (At-Tur: 21), then he said: ""And We did not diminish the fathers by what We gave the children."
"1451","[AI-translation] From Jabir, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) say: ""The people of Paradise eat and drink therein, and they do not spit, nor urinate, nor defecate, nor blow their noses."" They said: ""Then what about the food?"" He said: ""Belching and sweat like the sweat of musk. They are inspired to glorify and praise just as they are inspired to breathe."
"1452","[AI-translation] From Abdullah ibn Qays, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The people of the Fire weep until, if ships were run in their tears, they would flow; and they weep blood, meaning in place of tears."
"1453","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), who said: ""The lightest of the people of the Fire in torment on the Day of Resurrection is a man for whom two sandals of fire will be fashioned, from which his brain will boil on the Day of Resurrection."
"1454","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The first group to enter Paradise will be in the image of the moon on the night of the full moon. Then those who follow them will be upon the most intensely shining star in the sky; they do not urinate, nor defecate, nor blow their noses, nor spit. Their combs are of gold, their sweat is musk, their incense-burners are of aloes-wood, and their wives are the fair maidens with wide beautiful eyes. Their natures are upon the nature of one man, upon the image of their father Adam, sixty cubits in height."
"1455","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), who said: ""Indeed, the Hamim (scalding water) is poured over their heads, and it penetrates until it reaches his insides, melting what is in his belly until it passes out from his feet—and that is the melting—then he is restored as he was."
"1456","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Indeed, the Houris in Paradise sing, saying: 'We are the beautiful Houris, we are destined for noble husbands.'"
"1457","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, he said: It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Shall we have relations with our wives in Paradise?"" He said: ""Indeed, a man will have relations with a hundred virgins in a single day."
"1458","[AI-translation] From Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: ""Indeed, a man among the people of the Fire grows so large for the Fire that a molar from among his molars will be like Uhud."
"1459","[AI-translation] Ash'ari, he said: I heard my father, facing the enemy, say: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: 'Indeed, the swords are the keys to Paradise.'"" A man of shabby appearance said to him: ""Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)?"" He said: ""Yes."" So he drew his sword, broke its scabbard, turned to his companions, and said: ""I convey peace upon you."" Then he advanced toward the enemy and fought until he was killed."
"1460","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Utbah bin Ghazwan from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: The enormous rock is cast from the edge of Jahannam and falls in it for seventy years without reaching its bottom."
"1461","[AI-translation] Rahman bin Shibl from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: The wicked are the people of the Fire. It was said, ""O Messenger of Allah, who are the wicked?"" He said: Women. A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers, our sisters, and our wives?"" He said: Yes, but when they are given, they do not give thanks, and when they are tested, they are not patient."
"1462","[AI-translation] Narrated from Qays bin 'Abbad who said: We said to 'Ammar, ""Tell us about your fighting—was it an opinion you held, for an opinion may be right or wrong, or was it a covenant the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) made to you?"" He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) did not make any covenant to us that he did not make to all the people at large. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: In my Ummah there are twelve hypocrites who will not enter Jannah and will not find its scent until the camel passes through the eye of the needle. Eight of them, the Dubaylah will suffice you: a lamp of fire that appears on their shoulders until it bursts forth in their chests."
"1463","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: In Jannah there is a tree where a rider upon a swift, well-trained horse would travel for a hundred years without crossing it. This comes from the hadith of Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurairah, and Sahl bin Sa'd, and Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"1464","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: In Jannah there is a market they will visit every Friday; in it are dunes of musk. The north wind will blow and scatter musk upon their faces and garments, so they will increase in beauty and elegance. They will return to their families having increased in beauty and elegance, and their families will say to them: By Allah, you have increased in beauty and elegance since we left you. They will say: And by Allah, you too have increased in beauty and elegance since we left you."
"1465","[AI-translation] Harith bin Juz' Al-Zubaidi, a companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), he narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family): In the Fire are snakes like the necks of Bactrian camels; they will bite a single bite, the heat of which will be felt for forty autumns. And in it are scorpions like hobbled mules; they will sting a single sting, the heat of which will be felt for forty autumns."
"1466","[AI-translation] Narrated from Jabir bin 'Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: A people will be brought out of the Fire, having been burnt in it except for the circles of their faces, until they enter Jannah."
"1467","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Bakr bin Abu Musa bin Qais from his father from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: The believer will have in Jannah a tent of a single hollowed pearl, its length being sixty miles. The believer will have family members in it; the believer will go around them and they will not see one another."
"1468","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: The distance between the two leaves of the gate of Jannah is a journey of forty years."
"1469","[AI-translation] Narrated from Samurah bin Jundub that he heard the Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) saying: Among them are those whom the Fire will take up to their ankles, and among them are those whom the Fire will take up to their knees, and among them are those whom it will take up to their waist, and among them are those whom it will take up to their neck."
"1470","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to the Jews: I am going to ask them about the soil of Paradise, and it is white darikah. So he asked them, and they said: It is a loaf of bread, O Abu al-Qasim. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The loaf of bread is from darik."
"1471","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, elevated to the Prophet: ""The people of Paradise, their combs are of gold, and their censers are of aloe-wood."
"1472","Abdullah ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: ""The first group to enter Paradise will be the poor emigrants, those who serve as a shield against calamities. When they are commanded, they hear and obey. And if one of them has a need from the ruler, it will not be fulfilled for him until he dies while it is still in his heart. And indeed Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will call out to Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, and it will come with its adornments and beauty. Then He will say: 'Where are My servants who fought in My cause, were killed, were harmed in My cause, and strove in My cause? Enter Paradise.' So they will enter it without reckoning. And the angels will come and prostrate, and they will say: 'Our Lord, we glorify You with praise night and day, and we sanctify You. [Why do You favor] these whom You have preferred over us?' So the Lord, Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'These are those who fought in My cause and were harmed in My cause.' Then the angels will enter upon them from every gate [saying]: 'Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured. And excellent is the final home.' (Quran 13:24)"""
"1473","[AI-translation] Khudri from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: The first group to enter Paradise will be in the image of the moon on the night of the full moon, and the second group in the color of the most brilliant star in the sky. Every man among them will have two wives, upon each wife will be seventy garments, such that the marrow of her shins will be visible from behind them."
"1474","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah, elevated to the Prophet: Buthan is upon a water channel from the water channels of Paradise."
"1475","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: While I was journeying in Paradise, a river was presented to me whose two banks were domes of hollowed pearl. I said to the angel: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Al-Kawthar which Allah has given you. He said: Then he struck his hand into the clay and extracted musk. Then Sidrat al-Muntaha was raised for me, and I saw near it a great light."
"1476","[AI-translation] Awdi, who said: Mu'adh bin Jabal stood among us and said: O Banu Awd! I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: You know the return to Allah, then to Paradise or to the Fire, and an abode with no departure, and an eternity with no death, in bodies that do not die."
"1477","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: Three whose eyes will not see the Fire on the Day of Resurrection: an eye that wept from the fear of Allah, an eye that stood guard in the path of Allah, and an eye that lowered its gaze from the prohibitions of Allah."
"1478","[AI-translation] Sulami, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: Paradise has eight gates, and the Fire has seven gates."
"1479","[AI-translation] Samit that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Paradise has one hundred degrees; between every two degrees is a journey of one hundred years. And Affan said: Like the distance between the heaven and the earth. Al-Firdaus is its highest degree, and from it emerge the four rivers, and the Throne is above it. And when you ask Allah—Blessed and Exalted is He—ask Him for Al-Firdaus."
"1480","Al-Silsila-tu-Ahadees-e-Sahiha Hadees: 1480 Arabic Hadees:"
"1481","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Umamah from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, who said: A man entered Paradise, and he saw written on its gate: Charity is with ten times its like, and a loan is with eighteen."
"1482","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""I entered Paradise, and there I was with a palace of gold. I said: 'For whom is this palace?' They said: 'For a young man of Quraysh.' I thought I was he, so I said: 'And who is he?' They said: 'For Umar bin al-Khattab.'"" (He said: ""Were it not for what I knew of your jealousy, I would have entered it."" Umar said: ""Would I be jealous against you, O Messenger of Allah?"")"
"1483","[AI-translation] From Aishah, raised to the Prophet: ""I entered Paradise and I saw for Zayd bin Amr bin Nufayl two degrees."
"1484","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, was asked: ""What is al-Kawthar?"" He said: ""That is a river Allah has given me, meaning in Paradise, whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. In it are birds whose necks are like the necks of slaughtered camels."" Umar said: ""Indeed, these are tender."" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Eating them is more tender than them."
"1485","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""The children of the Muslims in Paradise will be cared for by Ibrahim, peace be upon him."
"1486","[AI-translation] Aziz bin al-Mukhtar from Abdullah ad-Danaj: I witnessed Abu Salamah bin Abd al-Rahman sitting in a mosque during the time of Khalid bin Abdullah bin Khalid bin Asid. He said: Al-Hasan came and sat by him, and we conversed. Abu Salamah said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""The sun and the moon are two oxen coiled in the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."" Al-Hasan said: ""What is their sin?"" He said: ""I am only narrating to you from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family."" So al-Hasan remained silent."
"1487","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hassan: I said to Abu Hurayrah: ""Two sons of mine have died, so will you not narrate to me a hadith from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, to comfort our souls regarding our dead?"" He said: He said: ""Yes. Their little ones are the da'āmīṣ of Paradise. One of them meets his father—or he said: his parents—and takes hold of his garment—or he said: his hand—just as I am taking hold of the edge of your garment here. He will not desist—or he said: he will not cease—until Allah enters him and his father into Paradise."
"1488","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""Two groups from the people of the Fire I have not seen: a people with whips like the tails of cows with which they strike the people, and women who are clothed yet naked, inclining and causing others to incline, their heads like the leaning humps of Bactrian camels. They will not enter Paradise, nor will they find its scent, and indeed its scent is found from a distance of such and such."
"1489","[AI-translation] Khudri from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: ""Tuba is a tree in Paradise, a distance of a hundred years; the garments of the people of Paradise come out of its sheaths."
"1490","[AI-translation] Salami: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, when a Bedouin came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I hear you mention a tree in Paradise, and I do not know of anything in the world with more thorns than it,"" meaning the Talh tree. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Indeed, Allah makes in place of every thorn (meaning from the Talh tree in Paradise) the like of the testicle of a castrated goat—meaning: the castrated—in it are seventy types of food, the color of one not resembling the color of another."
"1491","[AI-translation] Narrated Samurah, raised to the Prophet: ""Al-Firdaws is the highest elevation of Paradise, and it is its middle and its best."
"1492","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: The legs of my minbar are fixed in Paradise."
"1493","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Every inhabitant of the Fire will see his seat in Paradise and will say, ""If only Allah had guided me,"" so it will be a regret upon them. He said: And every inhabitant of Paradise will see his seat in the Fire and will say, ""Had it not been that Allah guided me,"" so it will be gratitude for him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) recited: ""Lest a soul should say, 'Alas, my regret over what I neglected in regard to Allah...'"" (Az-Zumar: 56)."
"1494","[AI-translation] Bahili passed by Khalid bin Yazid bin Muawiyah, so he asked him about the softest statement he had heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: Verily, all of you will enter Paradise except the one who strays from Allah like the straying of a camel from its people."
"1495","[AI-translation] Miqdam bin Madikarib from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) who said: The martyr has with Allah qualities: 1- He is forgiven in the first gush of his blood. 2- He is shown his seat in Paradise. 3- He is adorned with the garment of faith. 4- He is married to (seventy-two wives) from the Hur al-Ayn. 5- He is protected from the torment of the grave. 6- He is secure from the Great Terror. 7- A crown of dignity is placed upon his head, one ruby of which is better than the world and whatever is in it. 8- He intercedes for seventy people of his household."
"1496","[AI-translation] Ashari, elevated to the Prophet: If a stone were thrown into Jahannam, it would fall for seventy autumns before reaching its bottom."
"1497","[AI-translation] From Sad bin Abi Waqqas from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) he said: If what is equal to a fingernail of what is in Paradise were to appear, it would adorn whatever is between the ends of the heavens and the earth. And if a man from the inhabitants of Paradise were to look out and his bracelets were to appear, they would eclipse the light of the sun just as the sun eclipses the light of the stars."
"1498","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: If there were in this mosque one hundred (thousand) or more, and in it was a man from the Fire who exhaled and his breath touched them, the mosque and whoever is in it would burn up."
"1499","Shurayh ibn Ubayd said: Thawban fell ill in Hims, and Abd Allah ibn Qurt al-Azdi was its governor. He did not visit him. A man from the Kalb tribe entered to visit Thawban. Thawban said to him: ""Can you write?"" He said: ""Yes."" He said: ""Write."" So he wrote to the trustworthy Abd Allah ibn Qurt: ""From Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. As for what follows: If Moses and Jesus, peace be upon them, had a freed slave in your presence, you would have visited him."" Then he folded the letter and said to him: ""Will you deliver it to him?"" He said: ""Yes."" So the man went with his letter and handed it to Ibn Qurt. When he read it, he stood up in alarm. The people said: ""What is the matter with him? Has something happened?"" He came to Thawban until he entered upon him, visited him, and sat with him for a while. Then he stood up. Thawban grabbed his cloak and said: ""Sit until I narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard him say: 'Seventy thousand from my Ummah will enter Paradise without account and without punishment. With each thousand, seventy thousand.'"""
"1500","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: There is nothing of Paradise on earth except three things: the planting of the Ajwah, birds that descend into the Euphrates every day from the blessing of Paradise, and the Stone."
"1501","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, suspended: There is nothing in Paradise resembling (what is) in the world except the names."
"1502","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: A servant does not seek refuge from the Fire seven times in a day except that the Fire says: ""O Lord! Your servant so-and-so has sought refuge from me, so grant him refuge."" And a servant does not ask Allah for Paradise seven times in a day except that Paradise says: ""O Lord! Your servant so-and-so has asked me, so enter him into Paradise."
"1503","[AI-translation] From Zayd ibn Arqam who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a journey, and we alighted at a place, and I heard him say: ""You are but a part of a hundred thousand parts of those from my Ummah who will come to me at the Hawd. How many were you that day?"" He said: Seven hundred or eight hundred."
"1504","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""I have not seen the like of the Fire, its fleer sleeps, nor the like of Paradise, its seeker sleeps."
"1505","[AI-translation] Miqdam, raised to the Prophet: There is no one who dies as a miscarried infant nor of old age—and people are in between that—except that he will be resurrected a son of thirty years. So if he is among the people of Paradise, he will be upon the form of Adam, the appearance of Yusuf, and the heart of Ayyub. And whoever is among the people of the Fire, they will be made huge and enlarged like mountains."
"1506","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: ""There is none among you except that he has two dwellings: a dwelling in Paradise and a dwelling in the Fire. So if he dies and enters the Fire, the people of Paradise inherit his dwelling. That is His saying, the Exalted: 'It is they who are the inheritors.' (Al-Mu'minun: 10)"
"1507","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""My minbar is upon a water-channel of the water-channels of Paradise."
"1508","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: ""Whoever fasts the entire year, Hellfire will be narrowed for him like this,"" and he interlocked ninety."
"1509","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: ""Whoever enters Paradise will enjoy bliss, he will not be miserable, his clothes will not wear out, and his youth will not perish."
"1510","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: ""The place of a whip of one of you in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it."" And he recited: Aal 'Imran 185."
"1511","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that it was said to him: ""Will one have intercourse in Paradise?"" He said: ""Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, with a thrust, a thrust. And when he withdraws from her, she returns purified, a virgin."
"1512","[AI-translation] He said, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: ""Sleep is the brother of death, and the people of Paradise do not sleep."
"1513","Mujahid said: Ibn Abbas said: ""Do you know the vastness of Hell?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""Yes, by Allah, you do not know that the distance between the earlobe of one of them and his shoulder is a journey of seventy autumns, in which valleys of pus and blood flow."" I said: ""Rivers?"" He said: ""No, rather valleys."" Then he said: ""Do you know the vastness of Hell?"" I said: ""No."" He said: ""Yes, by Allah, you do not know. Aisha informed me that she asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) about His saying: 'And the earth entirely will be within His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand' (Az-Zumar: 67). So where will the people be on that day, O Messenger of Allah? He said: They will be on the Bridge over Hell."""
"1514","[AI-translation] Khudri: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand my soul is, you will all enter Paradise, except those who refuse and stray away from Allah like the straying of a camel."" They said, ""And who would refuse to enter Paradise?"" He said, ""Whoever obeys me enters Paradise, and whoever disobeys me has refused."
"1515","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The men and women boasted. Abu Hurairah said: ""The women are more numerous than the men in Paradise."" 'Umar bin Al-Khattab looked at the people and said: ""Do you not hear what Abu Hurairah is saying?"" Abu Hurairah said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say regarding the first group to enter Paradise: Their faces will be like the moon on the night of Badr, and the second group like the brightest star in the sky. Each of them will have two wives, the marrow of whose shins will be visible from behind the flesh, and there is no bachelor in Paradise."
"1516","[AI-translation] Yamani: The Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Ibrahim is the Khalil (friend) of Allah, 'Isa is the Word and Spirit of Allah, and Musa spoke to Allah directly. So what have you been given, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""All the children of Adam will be under my banner on the Day of Resurrection, and I will be the first for whom the gates of Paradise are opened."
"1517","[AI-translation] Narrated 'Umarah bin Khuzaimah: While we were with 'Amr bin Al-'As in Hajj or 'Umrah, (we came across a woman wearing garments, having signet rings, and she had spread her hand over the howdah). He said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) in this mountain pass, he said: ""Look, do you see anything?"" We said: ""We see crows, among which is a crow with a red beak and red legs."" The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""No women will enter Paradise except those who are like this crow among the crows."
"1518","Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reported: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""A man from the people of Paradise will be brought, and Allah will say to him: 'O son of Adam! How did you find your dwelling?' He will say: 'O Lord! The best dwelling.' He will say: 'Ask and wish.' He will say: 'What do I ask and wish for except that You return me to the world so that I may be killed in Your cause ten times, because of what he sees of the virtue of martyrdom.' (And in another narration: 'because of the honor [he sees].')And a man from the people of Hellfire will be brought, and Allah will say to him: 'O son of Adam! How did you find your dwelling?' He will say: 'O Lord! The worst dwelling.' He will say (the Lord, Mighty and Majestic) to him: 'Would you ransom yourself from it with the fill of the earth in gold?' He will say: 'O Lord! Yes.' He will say: 'You have lied. I asked you for less than that and easier, but you did not do it.' Then he will be returned to the Fire."""
"1519","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas bin Malik: Harithah bin Suraqah went out as a scout and an arrow struck and killed him. His mother said: ""O Messenger of Allah! You know Harithah's place in my heart. If he is in Paradise, I will be patient, otherwise you will see what I will do!"" He said: ""O Umm Harithah! It is not a single Paradise, but many Paradises, and Harithah is in the best of them"" or he said: ""in the highest of Firdaus."
"1520","[AI-translation] Hasan: An old woman came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah to enter me into Paradise."" He said: ""O Umm So-and-so! No old woman enters Paradise."" She turned away weeping. He said: ""Tell her that she will not enter it while she is an old woman, for Allah the Almighty says: 'Indeed, We have produced them in a new creation, And made them virgins, Loving [their husbands] and of equal age' (Al-Waqi'ah)."
"1521","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Wa'il: It was said to Usamah: ""If only you went to So-and-so"" - in another narration: 'Uthman - ""and spoke to him"" - in the other narration he added: ""and what would he do?"" He said: ""Do you think I would not speak to him except to make you hear?! I speak to him in secret, without opening a door that I would be the first to open, and I do not say to a man, if he is an Amir over me, that he is the best of people, because of something I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family)."" They said: ""And what did you hear him say?"" He said: ""I heard him say: 'A man will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and cast into the Fire, and his intestines will spill out (in a narration: the intestines of his belly) into the Fire, and he will circle around as a donkey circles around its millstone. The people of the Fire will gather around him and say: ""O So-and-so! What is the matter with you? Did you not use to enjoin good and forbid evil?"" He will say: ""I used to enjoin good and not do it, and forbid you from evil and do it.""'"
"1522","[AI-translation] Khudri, attributed to the Prophet: ""Whoever has a mustard seed's weight of faith in his heart will be taken out of the Fire."
"1523","[AI-translation] Khudri, attributed to the Prophet: ""A neck will emerge from the Fire, speaking and saying: 'I have been entrusted today with three: every obstinate tyrant, whoever set up a partner with Allah, and whoever killed a soul unjustly.' It will fold around them and cast them into the depths of Jahannam."
"1524","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise will enter Paradise, and whatever Allah Almighty wills will remain of it. Then Allah the Almighty will create for it, meaning a creation, until He fills it."
"1525","[AI-translation] Suddi who said: I asked Murrah al-Hamdani about the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. So he narrated to me that 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud narrated to them from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, who said: ""The people (all of them) will enter the Fire, then they will depart from it according to their deeds (so the first of them will be like the flash of lightning, then like the passing of the wind, then like the galloping of a horse, then like a rider, then like the running of a man, then like their walking)."
"1526","[AI-translation] Narrated from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: Allah will say to the one with the lightest punishment among the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection: (""O son of Adam! How did you find your resting place?"" He will say: ""An evil resting place."" It will be said to him:) ""If you had the world and whatever is in it, would you ransom yourself with it?"" He will say: ""Yes."" He will say: (""You have lied."") ""I wanted from you something easier than this while you were in the loins—and in a narration: the back—of Adam: that you do not associate (anything with Me) (and I will not enter you into the Fire), but you refused anything but polytheism."" So he will be ordered to the Fire."
